<title>PERU: Peru raises private sector minimum wage 13.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Peru raises private sector minimum wage 13.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Peruvian government decreed Tuesday a second hike this month in the minimum private sector wage, raising the basic salary to a monthly 300 soles ($113), up 13.2 percent from the current minimum of 265 soles ($100).</p>
<p>Until April, the private sector minimum wage was 215 soles per month.</p>
<p>The latest decree, published in the government's official gazette, will go into effect May 1.</p>
<p>The decree did not give any reason for the increase.</p>
<p>The government estimates this year's cumulative consumer price inflation will be below 10 percent, down from 11.8 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
</text>
